  "findings": [
    "VFTuning.c lines 146-162: query 0x10, 1-based point selector, ratio low byte and 11-bit offset at bit21.",
    "VFTuning.c lines 305-339: point set 0x11 submits only the 11-bit offset shifted left by 21; other payload bits are zero.",
    "The legacy domain programming in VFTuning.c lines 255-297 is separate from the point payload and is not copied into the new setter.",
    "FSP core and ring arrays contain 15 entries; this is a candidate bound, not a supported-point count on every processor.",
    "CpuData.c includes older client families through Alder Lake; it is not a Raptor Lake-S hardware validation certificate."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Profile scope remains the existing original-derived GenuineIntel family6/modelB7 client path.",
    "Default-domain gating is a conservative implementation policy; no assertion is made that all other combinations are invalid in firmware.",
    "No setting of command0x15, no global configuration reset, no per-physical-core or Xeon profile restoration.",
    "Synthetic tests do not establish physical voltage, curve-wide effects or stability."
  ]
